summary:
  The members' levels are asked for after the recorder has been started
  instead of before it.

history:
  It looks like free time: the recorder needs its warm-up anyway. But the
  slots are cut out of the capture by the schedule, counted from where
  the capture begins, and the clock the players are held to starts after
  the queries. Everything the queries take sits in the capture ahead of
  the first slot, so every member lands that much late in its own window.
  A few milliseconds are the same for all and cancel. One query that runs
  into its three-second timeout pushes every member out of its slot and
  into the next one's.

target:
  package/contents/ui/calibrate.py

find:
      volumes = [str(int(_ultra_volume_for(sink, trim))) for sink, _lag in members]
      rec = tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=".wav", delete=False).name
      try:
          rp = subprocess.Popen(recorder_args(mic, rec), stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)

replace:
      rec = tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=".wav", delete=False).name
      try:
          rp = subprocess.Popen(recorder_args(mic, rec), stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
          volumes = [str(int(_ultra_volume_for(sink, trim))) for sink, _lag in members]

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_calibrate.py::test_every_level_is_asked_for_before_the_capture_begins.
  Line-neutral.
